<section class="page-hero"><span class="pub-kicker">Control and trust</span><h1>Clear permissions.<br>Visible decisions.</h1><p>StockChief works from recorded business facts and the authority you configure. Review a prepared action and its consequences before giving approval where required.</p></section><section class="truth-section"><div><span class="pub-kicker">Your approval rules</span><h2>See what will change<br>before it changes.</h2><p>Stock movements, purchasing, messages and financial actions have their own permissions and approval paths. A connected account grants API access; your business authority determines which supported work may proceed.</p><p>Missing facts, conflicts and unresolved outcomes stay available for review. Ask can explain the records behind a result.</p><a class="pub-text-link" href="/demo">Explore the actual product →</a></div><figure class="truth-screen"><img src="/demo/ask.png?v=<%= assetVersion %>" alt="Actual StockChief answer with supporting business records" width="1440" height="900"><figcaption>Controlled demonstration records in the current application.</figcaption></figure></section><section class="trust-principles"><article><b>01</b><h2>Recorded business evidence</h2><p>Stock, orders and financial records stay linked to the operations that created them.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h2>Protected connection keys</h2><p>Provider credentials are encrypted at rest and excluded from ordinary record and support inspection views.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h2>Business-level access</h2><p>Membership and permissions scope operational requests to the correct business.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h2>Duplicate protection</h2><p>Supported workflows use transaction and idempotency checks. Uncertain provider outcomes can require review before another attempt.</p></article><article><b>05</b><h2>Customer-approved support access</h2><p>Approve the areas and duration of read-only support inspection, and revoke access when you choose. Inspection is audited.</p></article><article><b>06</b><h2>Your connected accounts</h2><p>Merchant payments and postage use the accounts you connect. Provider permissions and supported capabilities still apply.</p></article></section><section class="truth-final"><h2>See the records<br>behind the work.</h2><div class="pub-actions"><a class="pub-btn" href="/demo">Watch the actual product</a><a class="pub-btn pub-btn--secondary" href="/privacy">Read the privacy notice</a></div></section>
